  "answer_text": "# Welch Allyn Ophthalmology Tools\n\nWelch Allyn is a globally recognized manufacturer of medical diagnostic equipment, offering a comprehensive portfolio of ophthalmic instruments such as **ophthalmoscopes**, **retinoscopes**, and **vision screeners**. Here is an overview of their key ophthalmology tools:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 1. PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope\nThe **Welch Allyn PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope** is a wide-view instrument designed to enhance patient assessments. It features long-lasting LED lamps, DuraShock\u2122 technology for durability, and new **Quick Eye\u2122 alignment technology** that helps direct the patient's gaze for faster, easier exams. Two lights on the patient side help guide their gaze for better optic disc alignment.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 2. Standard Direct Ophthalmoscope (Model 11720-L)\nThe **Welch Allyn 11720-L Ophthalmoscope** is a standard direct ophthalmoscope available for eye examination. It is widely used in clinical and educational settings.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd26 3. Streak Retinoscope (Model 18245)\nWelch Allyn offers **retinoscopes** as part of their full range of ophthalmic equipment. The **Welch Allyn 18245 Streak Retinoscope** is used for objective refraction and determining refractive errors.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcf1 4. iExaminer SmartBracket System\nThe **Welch Allyn iExaminer SmartBracket** allows clinicians to capture and share eye images when paired with a smart device and the iExaminer Pro App. This enables digital documentation directly from the ophthalmoscope.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d 5. Transilluminator (Model 41100)\nThe **Welch Allyn 41100 Transilluminator** is used for ocular and tissue illumination during eye and physical examinations.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc76 6. Spot Vision Screener\nThe **Spot Vision Screener** is a handheld, portable device designed to help quickly and easily detect vision issues in patients as young as **six months**. Welch Allyn vision screening devices are designed to be easy to use and accurate, and can be used by healthcare professionals in schools, doctor's offices, and other settings.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udda5\ufe0f 7. RetinaVue 700 Imager\nThe **RetinaVue 700 Imager** makes retinal imaging and retinal exams simple and affordable in primary care, as the latest addition to the RetinaVue care delivery model family.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0b 8. Power Handles & Charging Systems\nAll portable ophthalmic sets now include ophthalmoscopes with **long-lasting LED illumination**. Welch Allyn also offers the **3.5V Premium Lithium-Ion Plus USB Rechargeable Power Handle** and a **Universal Desk Charger** to support all handheld instruments.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccb Summary Table\n\n| Tool | Primary Use |\n|------|-------------|\n| PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope | Wide-field fundus exam |\n| Direct Ophthalmoscope (11720-L) | Standard eye exam |\n| Streak Retinoscope (18245) | Objective refraction |\n| iExaminer SmartBracket | Digital image capture |\n| Transilluminator (41100) | Ocular illumination |\n| Spot Vision Screener | Pediatric/adult vision screening |\n| RetinaVue 700 Imager | Retinal imaging |\n| Rechargeable Power Handles | Power source for instruments |\n\n---\n\nWelch Allyn (now under **Hillrom/Baxter**) remains a trusted brand for both primary care providers and eye care specialists. Would you like more details on any specific tool?",
